  "rationale": "Only mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin are deployed, so all patched_*, segmented and mfa_user flags are false. The attacker can still get deep into the network: exploit_web gives foothold_web; pivot_internal gives reach_internal because the network is not segmented; steal_user_cred gives stolen_user; auth_appserver, auth_apiserver and auth_ciserver give footholds because mfa_user is off; kerberoast gives stolen_admin; and escalate_ciserver followed by leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin. However, auth_dc and auth_adfs both require NOT mfa_admin, so foothold_dc, foothold_adfs, admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. Every exfiltration path needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of those needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, which require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). That condition is false because mfa_dbadmin is deployed and admin_dc and admin_adfs are unreachable. No other technique grants those footholds, so exfiltrated is unreachable."
 },
